  "body": "Part of #3741. The entry sub-issue of #3741 uses this parameter.\n\n## The maintainer's words\n\n\"an outside cut would default to a ARC or straight approach in the plane of its cut, starting outside the stock boundary with a given value.\"\n\nFrom the #3741 comment: \"The approach starts outside the stock boundary by a given distance. That distance is a parameter with a default value.\" Pin (1) of that comment: \"the plunge XY is outside the stock box by at least the tool radius plus the approach distance\".\n\n## What happens\n\nNo such parameter exists. `crates/motion/src/approach.rs` (`Approach`, fields at `:80-110`, defaults at `:225-245`) has `arc_radius`, `arc_sweep`, `arc_xy` and `plunge_height`, but no distance from the stock edge. The MCP approach DTO (`crates/app/src/mcp/job.rs:292`, `crates/app/src/mcp/tools.rs:389`) has no such field.\n\n## Fix approach\n\n1. Add `approach_distance` (mm) to `Approach`. Recommended default: 2.0 mm, the same as `DEFAULT_PLUNGE_HEIGHT`. A value below 0 or not finite is refused when the command is made (\"Validate early\"). Record the default in `docs/decisions/`.\n2. Add it to the project file (`crates/app/src/project/approach.rs`, as `Option<f64>`, absent = default, so old files load unchanged), to the digest (`crates/app/src/operation/params/digest.rs`), and to `EditOperationParams` (undoable).\n3. Show it on the Lead in / Lead out page (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/lead_page.rs`) when Pass starts at is Inside or Outside.\n4. Add the MCP field under `links.approach` and to the `camcraft-mcp` skill table.\n\n## Pins (red first)\n\n- `approach_distance_round_trips`: save and load keep the value; a file without the field loads the default.\n- `approach_distance_edit_undoes`: an edit through `EditOperationParams` and its undo restore the previous value.\n- `mcp_sets_approach_distance`: the MCP tool sets and reads the field; a negative value is refused with a message.\n- A UI structural test: the row is present for Inside and Outside and absent for Auto.\n\nEffort `high`: a new parameter in several crates, with its command and MCP field. It changes posted G-code through the entry sub-issue.\n\nDone means: the parameter exists with its default in motion, the project file, the UI and MCP, and the four pins are green.\n",
